# Phase 1 Application Guide — Hands-On Tasks for Chapters 1–6
### Turning Notes Into Demonstrated Skill

> Reading the chapter notes gives you conceptual understanding. This file is the *doing* half. Each chapter below has: setup, tasks in order of difficulty, a way to verify you actually did it right (not just "ran a command"), and a deliverable to commit to GitHub. Do not skip tasks because you "understand the concept already" — the whole point of this roadmap is that watched-and-understood is not the same as done-and-verified.

**Environment assumption:** You have your Linux VM set up (Phase 0), Wireshark installed, and basic terminal comfort. If any of that's missing, stop and do Phase 0 first — everything below assumes it.

