## Chapter 6 — VLANs, Switching & Phase 1 Consolidation

> Chapter 6 doesn't have a Wireshark component (VLANs require actual switch hardware or Packet Tracer/GNS3 to observe directly) — its tasks are design-and-explain focused, plus the full Phase 1 integration test.

### Task 6.1 — Cisco Packet Tracer VLAN lab (45–60 min)
1. Open Packet Tracer (per your roadmap's Weeks 4–6 resource).
2. Build: 1 router, 2 switches, 4 PCs (2 per switch).
3. Configure 2 VLANs (e.g., VLAN 10 "Staff," VLAN 20 "Guest") — assign 2 PCs to each VLAN across both switches.
4. Configure the inter-switch link as a trunk port.
5. Test: use Packet Tracer's simulation mode to verify PCs in the same VLAN can ping each other, but PCs in different VLANs cannot (until you add inter-VLAN routing).
6. **Bonus:** Configure router-on-a-stick to allow controlled inter-VLAN routing, then re-test.

**Verification:** Screenshot the working ping test (same-VLAN success, cross-VLAN failure before routing, cross-VLAN success after routing configured).

### Task 6.2 — VLAN segmentation design for your home-lab diagram (20 min)
Using the topology you designed in Task 2.2, add VLAN segmentation:
1. Assign each device group to a VLAN (minimum 3 VLANs: e.g., Trusted, Guest, IoT/Servers)
2. Specify access vs. trunk ports on your diagram
3. Justify in 1 paragraph: why does separating Guest from Trusted matter from a security standpoint, not just an organizational one?

### Task 6.3 — Full Phase 1 integration narrative (30 min, no notes)
Write a single continuous narrative (not bullet points) explaining, end to end:
> "My laptop joins a Wi-Fi network. Walk through everything that happens, in order, until I successfully load a webpage — include DHCP, DNS, TCP, and where VLANs/switching fit into the picture."

This should be roughly 300–500 words, written from memory, then checked against your Chapter 1–6 notes for gaps.

### Task 6.4 — Subnetting speed retest (10 min, timed)
Re-run Task 3.4 (5 fresh subnetting problems). Compare your time/accuracy against your Week 3 baseline.

**Verification:** You should be meaningfully faster and more accurate than your Chapter 3 baseline. If not, this is a real gap — don't move to Phase 2 with shaky subnetting.

### Chapter 6 Deliverable
Files:
- `/phase1/tasks/chapter6-tasks.md` — Packet Tracer screenshots, VLAN design, integration narrative, subnetting retest comparison
- `/phase1/home-lab-network-diagram.md` (final version, incorporating VLANs)

### Chapter 6 Pass/Fail Check (this is the Phase 1 exit gate)
You pass Phase 1 entirely if:
- [ ] Task 6.3's narrative required no more than 1–2 lookups to complete
- [ ] Task 6.4 shows improvement over your Chapter 3 baseline
- [ ] Task 6.1's Packet Tracer lab actually demonstrates working VLAN isolation and (bonus) inter-VLAN routing
- [ ] You can explain every checklist item from the Chapter 6 notes' "Consolidated Review" section without notes

