## How to use this file

1. **Do NOT batch all tasks in one sitting per chapter.** Spread Chapter 3's tasks across the week — subnetting fluency needs spaced repetition, not a single cram session.
2. **Write your answers down, even the "obvious" ones.** The act of writing forces precision that just thinking "yeah I get it" doesn't.
3. **If a verification check fails, go back — don't push forward.** This is the single most important discipline in this roadmap. A shaky Chapter 3 will make Phase 6 (cloud subnetting) harder, and a shaky Chapter 6 will make Phase 7/8 segmentation reasoning harder.
4. **Commit after every chapter, not at the end of Phase 1.** Your roadmap explicitly values frequent commits over one big dump — this also gives you a real timestamped record of your pace, useful for the Week 6 subnetting speed comparison.

